      "inner_race": "BPFI",
      "outer_race": "BPFO"
    },
    "ranking_rule": "Among faults meeting the hit criterion: evidence tier (high > moderate > harmonic-only) first, then fundamental peak magnitude descending (a harmonic-only hit uses the 2x entry's magnitude), then absolute deviation_pct ascending, then fixed BPFO/BPFI/BSF/FTF order as the final deterministic tie-break. Classification is correct when the ranked-first fault maps to the label; a normal record is correct when no fault meets the criterion."
